:: WatchHunters [childhood]
# Weapons of the Hunt

You approach the area where several hunters are preparing their weapons. They check spears for straightness, sharpen stone points, and repair any damage from previous hunts.

One of the hunters, a man named <<if $language eq "proto-indo-european">>Koryos<<elseif $language eq "proto-uralic">>Metsästäjä<<else>>Anhur<</if>>, notices your interest.

"Curious about our tools, little one?" he asks with a smile. When you nod, he shows you the spear he's working on.

"This shaft must be straight and strong," he explains. "We find the best wood and dry it carefully. Then we attach the point - see how it's shaped to cut deeply?"

He demonstrates how the stone point is bound to the shaft with sinew and sealed with tree resin to keep it secure. Then he shows you other hunting tools - a throwing stick that can extend the range of a spear, a stone knife for skinning, and snares for catching small animals.

"Each tool has its purpose," he explains. "And each must be made with care, or it might fail when you need it most."

<<if gameUtils.hasSkillLevelIncreased("toolMaking")>>
  <div class="skill-message">
    <span class="skill-increase">Your tool making knowledge has improved!</span>
  </div>
<</if>>

<<link "Ask about hunting techniques">>
  <<set $skills.hunting += 0.1>>
  <<goto "HuntingTechniques">>
<</link>>

<<link "Ask to help prepare a simple tool">>
  <<set $skills.toolMaking += 0.2>>
  <<goto "HelpWithTools">>
<</link>>